  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The paper is a theoretical synthesis and does not present empirical data, quantitative measurements, or case study evaluations.",
      "what": "This theoretical paper synthesizes the historical evolution of temporary urbanism and adaptable cities, tracing how planning debates have shifted from rigid, permanent structures toward flexible, transient spatial uses.",
      "why": "It provides a conceptual framework that helps planners reconcile the tension between long-term master planning and the immediate, shifting needs of urban populations."
